      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Main results (Table 1, Figure 3). The large general LLMs beat most small open models, but the 4B TCAR reports the best score on every dataset except CLINC150, whose 150 intents make prompts average 18k tokens: 91.63 on HWU64, 96.70 on MINDS14, 91.58 on SGD and 93.98 F1 on QCloud, against GPT-5.1, Claude-Sonnet-4.5 and DeepSeek-v3.1-terminus. In a human-preference comparison on QCloud, the Refining Agent (built on DeepSeek-v3.1) wins human-preference comparisons against a single randomly chosen agent, most clearly on troubleshooting queries; for consultation queries one agent is usually enough. The figure's extracted labels give win rates of 27.0% and 63.0%, which by the caption are consultation and troubleshooting respectively.",
