      "content": "To systematically analyze the contribution of each component in TCAR, we conduct ablation studies\nalong three dimensions: reasoning capability, training strategy, and the source of RL initialization.\nEffect of Reasoning This experiment evaluates the impact of explicit reasoning chains[10] on routing\nperformance.\n• Without reasoning: The model performs direct classification prediction and outputs only Aq.\n• With reasoning: The model first generates Cq as an explicit and interpretable reasoning chain\nand then outputs the set of agents Aq.\nWe evaluated both settings on the public datasets and the",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Ablation studies on three factors. Reasoning: TCAR with a reasoning chain scores higher than without on all five datasets (Table 2), the largest gap on SGD, 91.58 against 84.96, which the authors read as better generalisation. RL: SFT followed by RL beats SFT alone on four datasets (Table 3), most on SGD, and raises recall on QCloud, curing SFT's tendency to output a single agent, though on CLINC150 it is marginally lower (91.25 against 91.32). Initialisation: RL started from a Slerp merge of five SFT models gives no clear gain in final scores (Table 4) but, in Figure 4, keeps higher entropy at similar reward, which the authors take as broader exploration. The block ends at the heading of the ablation summary.",
